Recommends: python3-gi,
            gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0,
            libnotify-bin
Description: live web dashboard for colcon builds
 Colcon Dashboard serves a single-page dashboard for a colcon
 workspace: a state-colored dependency graph with layered, force, and 3D
 layouts, a Gantt timeline, isolated per-package log panes with terminal
 colors, and CPU, RAM, and swap meters with a per-core heatmap.
 .
 One server per machine serves every workspace. The package enables
 it as a systemd user service for every user, so it starts at login.
 Chrome, Chromium, Edge, and Brave can install the dashboard as an app
 with its own window.
 .
 Colcon Dashboard in the applications menu (or colcon-dashboard --app)
 opens the dashboard in the browser. The optional tray icon shows the
 builds and starts and stops the server. It uses the recommended
 python3-gi and gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0 packages. The server sends desktop
 notifications through the recommended libnotify-bin package.
